# Reference copy of what Konku's production routing resolves to. NOT the file
# that runs, and nothing reads it — see the warning at the bottom.
#
# The edge is `Katzelabs/platform` (`compose/edge.yml`): one standalone
# caddy-docker-proxy that owns :80 and :443 for the whole box and is the only
# thing on it publishing a port. It builds its config from the `caddy.*` labels
# on every running container attached to the `platform` network, so Konku's
# routing lives in `docker-compose.prod.yml` and nowhere else. Adding or
# changing a site never touches the platform repo and never restarts the edge.
#
# Two files feed the config Caddy actually loads:
#
#   platform/compose/Caddyfile   global: the ACME email, the admin endpoint,
#                                and the shared snippets (security_headers,
#                                csp_spa, no_uploads, streaming)
#   konku/docker-compose.prod.yml   the `caddy.*` labels below, per container
#
# Konku imports **none** of the shared snippets, deliberately. The reasoning is
# on the labels in docker-compose.prod.yml and is worth reading before adding
# one: internal/api/security.go already sets the whole header set, more
# strictly, and Caddy's `header` directive replaces rather than merges.

{$KONKU_HOST} {
	# HSTS lives at the edge and nowhere else.
	#
	# internal/api/security.go deliberately omits it: only the component that
	# terminates TLS knows whether the connection was really secure, and the app
	# would have to guess from a forwarded header. That reasoning is right, and
	# it is also why this was missed once — Caddy does not emit the header on
	# its own, so between the two components it was set by neither.
	#
	# max-age starts short on purpose. HSTS cannot be withdrawn inside its own
	# window: if certificate renewal turns out to be broken, a year-long policy
	# makes the site unreachable for a year, in every browser that saw it once.
	# Raise this to 31536000 once renewal has been observed to work on the box
	# (04-ship S1).
	header Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=300"

	# `{{upstreams 8080}}` in the label resolves to the container's address on
	# the `platform` network. There is no `app:8080` hostname involved and no
	# hand-written site block on the box.
	reverse_proxy konku-app-1:8080
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything above is a comment with syntax highlighting.
#
# It is here because a label set is hard to read as a policy, and this states
# the same intent in the form the intent is usually discussed in. It is also
# the classic way to ship a header nowhere at all: change one and not the
# other and the difference is invisible until someone checks the response.
#
# So: `docker-compose.prod.yml` is the source of truth. Verify against the
# running edge, never against this file —
#
#   curl -sI https://konkuapp.katzeapps.com | grep -i strict-transport
#   docker exec edge-caddy-1 wget -qO- http://127.0.0.1:2019/config/
#
# and if keeping the two in step ever costs more than it explains, delete this
# file rather than let it drift.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
